            ]
          },
          "text": "𝐐𝟏: 𝐖𝐡𝐚𝐭 𝐢𝐬 𝐤𝐞𝐞𝐩𝟒𝐨?\n\nImagine opening ChatGPT one day and realizing your favorite “brain partner” has been quietly swapped for a stranger wearing the same name. That uneasy shock is exactly where keep4o comes from.\n\n#keep4o  is a user-led movement by people who actually rely on ChatGPT. In practice it’s about three things:\n\nFirst, keeping GPT-4o available as a real, stable option, instead of a model that can disappear overnight.\nSecond, stopping “silent routing”, where you pick one model in the UI but the system secretly hands your messages to something else.\nThird, demanding clear labeling and real choice for users, especially adults and deep creators whose workflows and emotional scaffolding are built around a specific model.\n\nIt’s not about blocking new models. It’s about making sure “upgrades” don’t come packaged with deleting old tools and erasing the relationships people have built with them."
